{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"tigerseye-molecular-chamois","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nREADME installation prose has stale dependency versions and ambiguous Git requirements. `pyproject.toml` defines the package contract. `pugnacious-soaplike-blackfish` records the decision to enforce Git 2.38 for development and CI without test skips.\n\n## Plan\n- Document the three base dependencies.\n- Correct the MCP extra to `mcp>=1.28.1,<2` with PyJWT cryptography support.\n- Describe Anthropic, Bedrock, OpenAI, and Google provider installation accurately.\n- State that Git is a runtime prerequisite.\n- State that Git 2.38 is the development and test floor and that the S3 repair path also needs `merge-tree --write-tree`.\n- Change documentation only. Do not modify packaging.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] README dependency claims match `pyproject.toml`.\n- [ ] Provider-extra guidance names the correct installation boundary for each provider.\n- [ ] Git guidance preserves the enforced contributor and CI floor without presenting it as a universal floor for every runtime path.\n- [ ] The S3 repair capability requirement remains discoverable.\n- [ ] Targeted README and documentation checks pass.\n- [ ] No dependency declaration or packaging file changes.","id":"c97b-ac47-1349-46fd","parent_id":"f7e4-4d33-f231-4774","priority":1,"tags":["documentation","f08b"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"F08B correct README installation contracts"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787417175257932001,"uuid":"7814634c-aac4-4cea-b7a1-b5c723a05f5b"}